## 1. Design Tokens

### 1.1 Color tokens

```css
/* Backgrounds */
--bg-primary:        #0B132B;   /* Deep midnight — page background */
--bg-surface:        #1C2541;   /* Cards, panels */
--bg-elevated:       #1F2A4A;   /* Modals, popovers, hover state on surface */
--bg-inset:          #060A1A;   /* Code blocks, deep recesses */

/* Accents */
--accent-cyan:       #00F5FF;   /* CTAs, active states, focus rings, status pulse */
--accent-cyan-dim:   #00B8C2;   /* Cyan hover/pressed state */
--accent-violet:     #6366F1;   /* Data viz, secondary highlights */
--accent-violet-dim: #4F46E5;   /* Violet hover */

/* Text */
--text-primary:      #F0F4FF;   /* Body, headings */
--text-secondary:    #A0AEC0;   /* Supporting text, labels */
--text-muted:        #6B7280;   /* Captions, metadata, timestamps */
--text-disabled:     #4A5568;
--text-on-cyan:      #0B132B;   /* Text on cyan buttons */

/* Semantic */
--success:           #10B981;   /* "Meeting booked", "Lead qualified" */
--warning:           #F59E0B;   /* "Awaiting approval", "Low confidence" */
--error:             #EF4444;   /* "Call failed", "Disconnected" */
--info:              #3B82F6;

/* Borders & dividers */
--border-subtle:     rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
--border-default:    rgba(255,255,255,0.12);
--border-strong:     rgba(255,255,255,0.20);
--focus-ring:        #00F5FF;
```

**Cyan usage rule:** Electric Cyan is reserved for CTAs, focus rings, status indicators, and icon highlights. **Never use cyan for body text or paragraph copy** — fails comfortable reading even when it passes contrast math.

### 1.2 Type scale

**Fonts loaded:** Montserrat (700, 800) for display headings only · Assistant (400, 600) for everything else.

| Token | Size | Line-height | Weight | Treatment |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `display` | 56px | 1.05 | 800 | Montserrat, `letter-spacing: 0.12em`, UPPERCASE |
| `h1` | 40px | 1.15 | 700 | Montserrat, `letter-spacing: 0.08em`, UPPERCASE |
| `h2` | 28px | 1.2 | 700 | Montserrat, normal case, normal tracking |
| `h3` | 20px | 1.3 | 600 | Assistant Semibold, normal case |
| `h4` | 16px | 1.4 | 600 | Assistant Semibold, normal case |
| `body` | 15px | 1.55 | 400 | Assistant Regular |
| `body-sm` | 13px | 1.5 | 400 | Assistant Regular |
| `caption` | 12px | 1.4 | 400 | Assistant Regular, `--text-muted` |
| `mono` | 13px | 1.5 | — | JetBrains Mono (for IDs, JSON, technical chips) |

**Rule:** uppercase + wide tracking applies **only to `display` and `h1`**. Everything else is normal case.

### 1.3 Spacing & radii

- Spacing scale: Tailwind defaults (`4 / 8 / 12 / 16 / 24 / 32 / 48 / 64`).
- Radii: `sm: 6px`, `md: 10px`, `lg: 16px`, `xl: 24px`, `full: 9999px`. Cards default to `lg`.

### 1.4 Motion tokens

```
--duration-fast:   150ms
--duration-base:   220ms
--duration-slow:   400ms
--duration-glow:   1600ms (looping pulse)
--ease-standard:   cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1)
--ease-emphasized: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1)
```

**Library:** Framer Motion for orchestrated animations (page transitions, list reorders, the Live Feed). Plain CSS for hover/focus micro-interactions.

**Accessibility:** every animation must respect `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` and fall back to opacity-only or instant transitions.

### 1.5 Elevation

- `elev-1`: `box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.4)` + 1px subtle border
- `elev-2`: `box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.45)` + 1px default border
- `elev-glow`: `box-shadow: 0 0 24px rgba(0,245,255,0.35)` — used **only** for Danie's active-state cards and CTA hover.

**No global glassmorphism.** `backdrop-filter: blur` is restricted to **at most two surfaces per page** (e.g., the floating chat dock, the top nav on scroll). Cards use solid `--bg-surface` + 1px borders for depth. This is a deliberate trade for 60fps scroll performance on dense dashboards.

